{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And He said: My Presence shall go, and I will give you rest.</b> The commentators disagree concerning the word 'My Presence' — whether it is a countenance of anger or a countenance of mercy. 'Shall go' implies the future, whereas Moses said, 'If Your Presence does not go' — in the present, immediately: 'do not bring us up from here.' This holds whether the meaning is that the anger shall depart from them at once, or whether the meaning is that the countenance of His mercy, blessed be He, shall go with them at once. And according to our way, He answered him on two matters at once: regarding what Moses had found astonishing — that He had not informed him that He would send His emissary with him to aid him — on this He said, <b>My Presence shall go</b>, as in 'and your presence goes in the midst' (II Samuel 17:11), for it is written, 'And YHWH spoke to Moses face to face,' and from those faces the light of His Presence, blessed be He, would go upon the face of Moses, and through this the Holy One, blessed be He, would provide him guidance as though the Name were going with him literally. And even though this influx comes only at intervals, nevertheless it would suffice for Moses to enable him to lead the people upward and to guide them on the way of YHWH — and this is what He said: <b>and I will give you rest.</b> And Moses said: this is simple, and I am not asking about this; for if the light of Your Presence does not go, surely do not bring us up from here, and without finding favor this matter is necessarily so, for we have no ascent at all without this. If so, my request returns to its place: what will You do for me on account of finding favor? And this is what he said: 'And by what shall it be known that I have found favor in Your eyes — I and Your people?' — that the favor shall extend from me also to Your people: 'by Your going with us' literally at all times, that You cleave to me through Your making known to me Your way, and in this alone 'we shall be distinguished — I and Your people — from all the people,' etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:25:11.031770458Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}